            <ArticleTitle>Use of long-term stable CsPbBr3 perovskite quantum dots in phospho-silicate glass for highly efficient white LEDs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11068-11071</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc06486a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the synthesis of CsPbBr3 QDs with great stability and high quantum yield in phospho-silicate glass, which was fabricated by using a heat-treatment approach, for white light emitting devices. QD glasses exhibited excellent photo- and thermal stability, and significantly prolonged the lifetime of light emitters under ambient air conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
